    "title": "Nobel-winning AI scientist John Jumper said he was leaving Google DeepMind for Anthropic, drawing praise from Google AI chief Demis Hassabis | Hindustan Times",
    "text": "Who John Jumper is and what he created\nJumper worked at Google DeepMind as a senior research scientist, and his departure from the company was considered surprising by CNBC. Jumper became well-known for being a co-inventor of AlphaFold, a system that has already made predictions about more than 200 million protein structures, according to CNBC. The same report says it has cut years off biological and medical research. Those are strong claims, so it is worth looking at the research behind them. There is a Nature study published in 2021, and Jumper is listed as the first author.",
    "summary": "Who John Jumper is and what he created Jumper worked at Google DeepMind as a senior research scientist, and his departure from the company was considered surprising by CNBC. Jumper became well-known for being a co-inventor of AlphaFold, a system that has already made predictions about more than 200 million protein structures, according to CNBC. The same report says it has cut years off biological and medical research. Those are strong claims, so it is worth looking at the research behind them. There is a Nature study published in 2021, and Jumper is listed as the first author.",
